* Relationships:
	+ Age is a measurement of the subject's age.
	+ Sex is a characteristic of the subject.
	+ Women of childbearing potential must have negative serum (Beta HCG) pregnancy tests.
	+ Women of childbearing potential must practice abstinence or use an acceptable form of contraception.
	+ Intrauterine device is a method of contraception.
	+ Barrier methods are a type of contraception.
	+ Spermicidal agent is a component of barrier methods.
	+ Postmenopausal course is a characteristic of women of childbearing potential.
	+ Surgical sterility is a characteristic of women of childbearing potential.
	+ Ideal Body Weight (IBW) is a measurement of the subject's weight.
	+ Table of "Desirable Weights of Adults" is a reference for calculating IBW.
	+ Metropolitan Life Insurance Company is the publisher of the Table of "Desirable Weights of Adults".
	+ Pre-study medical evaluation is a process of evaluating the subject's health.
	+ Physical examination is a part of the pre-study medical evaluation.
	+ Laboratory evaluation is a part of the pre-study medical evaluation.
	+ 12-lead ECG is a part of the pre-study medical evaluation.
	+ Hepatitis B test is a part of the pre-study medical evaluation.
